 },
 {
  "text": "A workshop supervisor has identified that students are at risk of eye injuries from metal swarf when filing. Using the hierarchy of control measures, discuss the range of controls that could be put in place, from most effective to least effective.",
  "type": "9 marks — Discuss / Analyse (Extended Response)",
  "marks": "Mastering: Works through the hierarchy systematically: Elimination — consider whether filing can be replaced by a process that produces less swarf (not always practical); Substitution — use a smoother file grade or a different process (limited effect on swarf); Engineering controls — fit an extraction hood over the filing area, use a vice to secure the workpiece (reduces swarf projection); Administrative controls — create a safe working procedure requiring goggles to be worn, train students on safe filing technique, mark a safe distance for bystanders; PPE — issue safety goggles as the last line of protection. Explains why higher levels are preferred and why PPE alone is insufficient. Reaches a conclusion. Secure: Covers all five levels; reasoning is present but one level lacks development. Developing: Covers three levels with some reasoning. Emerging: Lists PPE and one or two other measures without using the hierarchy structure."
 }
